# api/.dev.vars.example — local development secrets for the tenant Worker.
#
# `wrangler dev` (used by `npm run dev` and `npm run dev:local`) auto-loads a
# file named `.dev.vars` from this directory into `env`. Get started with:
#
#   cp api/.dev.vars.example api/.dev.vars
#
# NONE of the values below are required for `npm run dev:local` — that command
# runs in demo mode (auto-login, seeded data) and short-circuits email and AI.
# It only needs the `.dev.vars` file to exist. Uncomment a key here to exercise
# that one integration against a real service.
#
# This file holds LOCAL secrets only. Non-secret per-env config (APP_URL,
# TENANT_ID, STATE, PROVIDER, …) lives in wrangler.toml — see
# api/wrangler.example.toml. Production secrets are set with
# `wrangler secret put`, never here (see the "Secrets" note at the bottom of
# api/wrangler.example.toml).
#
# `.dev.vars` is gitignored; this `.dev.vars.example` is committed. Never put a
# real value in this example file.

# --- AI summaries & tagging (optional) --------------------------------------
# Direct Google Gemini key — used when AI_GATEWAY_ENABLED is not "true".
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. Leave unset to skip AI locally.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Cloudflare AI Gateway auth token — used instead of GEMINI_API_KEY when
# AI_GATEWAY_ENABLED=true (which also needs CF_ACCOUNT_ID and CF_AIG_GATEWAY as
# vars in wrangler.toml). Account-level token with the "AI Gateway Run" scope.
# CF_AIG_TOKEN=

# --- Login bot-check (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Turnstile keys for the real magic-link login flow. Demo mode skips
# login entirely, so these matter only when testing real login locally. The
# site key is public; the secret key is not. Cloudflare publishes always-pass
# test keys: https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/troubleshooting/testing/
# TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# --- Transactional email (optional) -----------------------------------------
# Only used when EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend (set in wrangler.toml). Demo mode and the
# default Cloudflare email provider do not use it. https://resend.com/api-keys
# RESEND_API_KEY=

# --- Local mode override (optional) -----------------------------------------
# Force demo auto-login under a plain `npm run dev`. `npm run dev:local` sets
# this for you, so you rarely need it here.
# DEMO_MODE=true
